# Authentication code is intended to require TWO approving reviews,
# not one, but that is not enforced today: this project currently has
# a single maintainer, and main's branch protection requires 0
# approving reviews. This file cannot express the two-review rule
# either way - GitHub's "Require approvals" count is a branch
# protection setting, not a CODEOWNERS one. Once a second maintainer
# exists, branch protection must be updated to require two approvals
# so the rule below is actually enforced rather than just documented
# here and in CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# It applies to:
#   crates/daycompass-server/src/auth/**
#   crates/daycompass-server/src/clientip.rs
#   crates/daycompass-server/src/ratelimit.rs
#   crates/daycompass-server/src/routes/auth.rs
#   crates/daycompass-server/src/routes/setup.rs
#   crates/daycompass-server/src/middleware.rs
#   crates/daycompass-server/migrations/** touching users, sessions or
#     setup_tokens
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md for what a reviewer should look for.
